# Beat: guided walk through bob/logfile against alice/app.desc.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc bob/logfile \
#       --script beats/app.desc
#
# The root type is not in alice/app.desc — it is Bob's own log envelope,
# which reproto recovered no schema for.  The session opens untyped.
# This beat names the structure by hand, enables heat cues, and follows
# the cues as far as alice/app.desc can take them.
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc bob/logfile \
#       --script beats/app.desc script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: The logfile, app.desc

steps:
  - text: |
      bob/logfile, opened against alice/app.desc.

      Larger than bob/capture.
      The root type is unknown — app.desc has no schema for the envelope.
      What we see is raw field numbers.

      👋 Press `1` to fold the top-level nodes.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - not:
        - visible: /1/1

  - text: |
      Cleaner view.

      Note the TRUNCATED_MESSAGE annotation.
      The logging process was probably killed mid-write — 1024 bytes missing.
      That is why protoc bailed out entirely.

      👋 Press `2` to see one level deeper.

    fold: ["/ 1"]
    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /1/1

  - text: |
      Each top-level field holds a similar submessage.
      Log entries — one per RPC call.

      The prefilled command below declares a synthetic type "Entry",
      marks field 1 as repeated, and names it "entries".

      👋 Press Enter to commit.

    fold: ["/ 2"]
    node: /
    search: "1 [{]  #@ message"
    command: override /:1 --as-new Entry --cardinality repeated --field-name entries
    advance_when:
      - type: /1 Entry

  - text: |
      👍 Entry is in place.

      Now let's enable heat cues.
      protolens will highlight where it recognizes known types.
      The brighter the cue, the more confident.

      👋 Press `i`.

    fold: ["/ 2"]
    node: /
    search: "entries [{]  #@ repeated Entry"
    advance_when:
      - heat_cues: findings

  - text: |
      Field 5 of the first entry has a bright heat cue.
      Hover over it — two candidates.

      SearchTextResponse matches what we saw in bob/capture.

      👋 Double-click the heat cue, then double-click SearchTextResponse.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2"]
    node: /1/4
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/4 google.maps.places.v1.SearchTextResponse

  - text: |
      👍 SearchTextResponse locked in.

      Field 4 has an amber cue — one candidate.
      SearchTextRequest. Makes sense: request + response pair.

      👋 Double-click the heat cue, then press Enter.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2"]
    node: /1/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/3 google.maps.places.v1.SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      👍 SearchTextRequest locked in.

      Field 2: a string. Looks like the RPC method name.
      Let's just rename it "rpc".

      👋 Press Enter to commit the prefilled command.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2"]
    node: /1/2
    select_line: true
    command: override Entry:2 --field-name rpc
    advance_when:
      - field_name: /1/2 rpc

  - text: |
      Field 1: hover the heat cue.
      Timestamp — fits a log entry.

      👋 Press `t`, choose Timestamp, press Enter to commit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/1
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/1 google.protobuf.Timestamp

  - text: |
      👌 Perfect.

      Now look at the 3rd entry — fields 6 and 7.
      Field 6 scores deeply negative 😨 and heat cues give nothing convincing 🤔.

      app.desc only knows the Places API.
      Fields 6 and 7 look like a different service entirely.

      👋 Press space to step.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      Before we go further, let's save our overrides.
      We do not want to redo this work.

      👋 Press Enter to save.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /3/3
    command: save-overrides alice/overrides
    advance_when:
      - file_exists: alice/overrides

  - text: |
      All done.
      
      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    command: quit
